abstract: >-
  The Structural Intelligence Framework (SIF) is a research architecture
  for organizing, locating, composing, governing, evaluating, and evolving
  heterogeneous intelligence capabilities. It proposes four functional
  domains, problem-capability dual maps, a structural precedent registry,
  universal naming, typing and relay, structural intelligence contracts,
  multi-intelligence adversarial validation, and evidence-governed structural
  growth. The initial release presents conceptual research and candidate
  specifications rather than a validated production implementation.
